# One systemd unit name per line, enabled under multi-user.target at build time.
#
# Only list units that EXIST in the image: either something a package you installed provides, or one
# of your own shipped via rootfs/etc/systemd/system/. A name with no unit behind it produces a dangling
# symlink and a failed boot job.
#
# You usually do NOT need to list a vendor agent's own service. Its package almost certainly enables
# itself through the normal Debian preset machinery during install.
#
# example-log-forwarder.service
